From 1ef749cd065e980fc6bd2d600be97737975e0a89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 17:37:43 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(setup): write a working user lefthook config so the
 workflow is reachable after init

Fresh forge init/setup left stage commands dead-ended on HOOKS_NOT_ACTIVE: lefthook's
postinstall drops a fully-commented stub lefthook.yml, which blocked Forge's copy
(guarded by a bare existence check), and the config Forge shipped referenced repo-internal
scripts/ a user project never has. Now Forge writes a minimal user config (pre-commit ->
.forge/hooks/check-tdd.js, pre-push -> npm test --if-present), overwriting only a
disposable stub and never a real config. Verified end-to-end: init -> hooks install ->
forge plan unblocked -> a real commit passes the TDD gate. (kernel c713fce7)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 CHANGELOG.md                               |  1 +
 lib/commands/setup.js                      | 60 ++++++++++++++---
 test/commands/lefthook-user-config.test.js | 78 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 131 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 test/commands/lefthook-user-config.test.js

